1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,500
Córdoba, Argentina. October 2020.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,500
NASA satellites spot fires like this from space.

3
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,900
Fire Watch turns 26 years of that
into one fire calendar.

4
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:10,800
Fire follows the seasons.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Old and new satellites count fire differently.

6
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:16,200
Fire Watch puts them on one scale.

7
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,400
October 2020:
2.4× the usual fire activity.

8
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:24,600
Tested on years it never saw,
the error drops from 75% to 16%.

9
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:29,500
A fire calendar for any place on Earth.
Fire Watch.
